\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The mesh laws are not the arc laws}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The [circle mesh](fdip-004H) is nearest-neighbor, with mass
squared #{\mu} independent of the number of vertices.
\ref{fdip-00B4} shows that one decimation step does not preserve
it. Those finite laws are not the cyclic arc laws on the
[dyadic index](fdip-00B6). The averages that follow are means in
the mesh field, whose raw covariance is the one recorded in
\ref{fdip-004I}.}
